  "id": "urn:visionflow:page:ba7f5acd6c32de9dac7517f72f80b0904a1008b78e73020e0be91263d1f93655",
  "title": "Agent Skill",
  "slug": "agent-skill",
  "public": true,
  "classIri": "urn:ngm:class:agent-skill",
  "domain": "artificial-intelligence",
  "definition": "An agent skill is a packaged, self-contained unit of procedural knowledge \u2014 a named bundle of instructions, and optionally scripts and reference resources \u2014 that an agent loads into its context on demand when a task matches the skill's trigger, and unloads afterwards. Rather than baking every capability into the base system prompt, a skill lets specialised know-how (how to run a deployment, audit prose, drive a browser) live as a discoverable, versioned artifact that is progressively disclosed only when relevant, keeping the working context small while giving the agent deep competence in whatever domain the current task demands.",
